<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wunü Mountain</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wunü Shan, Wunü Mountain City</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wunü Mountain is a flat-topped mountain near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huanren">Huanren</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, crowned by a stone-walled fortress of the Korean kingdom of Goguryeo. It is usually identified with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolbon">Jolbon</a>, the first capital founded according to tradition by Jumong in 37 BCE. The fortress is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> site of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capital-cities-and-tombs-of-the-ancient-koguryo-kingdom">Capital Cities and Tombs of the Ancient Koguryo Kingdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wunu-mountain.jpg" alt="Wunü Mountain" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Ndpy007 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%BA%94%E5%A5%B3%E5%B1%B1%E8%BF%9C%E6%99%AF.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
